#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/idaklu-jax-interface.ipynb:9
msgid "IDAKLU-JAX interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/idaklu-jax-interface.ipynb:11
msgid ""
"The IDAKLU-JAX interface requires that PyBaMM is installed with the "
"`optional JAX solver enabled <https://docs.pybamm.org/en/stable/source/"
"user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.html#optional-jaxsolver>`__ (``pip "
"install pybamm[jax]``) and requires at least Python 3.10."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/idaklu-jax-interface.ipynb:13
msgid ""
"PyBaMM provides two mechanisms to interface battery models with JAX. The "
"first (JaxSolver) implements PyBaMM models directly in native JAX, and as "
"such provides the greatest flexibility. However, these models can be very "
"slow to compile, especially during their initial run, and can require large "
"amounts of memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/idaklu-jax-interface.ipynb:15
msgid ""
"The second (the IDAKLU-Jax interface) instead provides a JAX-compliant "
"interface to the IDAKLU solver. IDAKLU is a fast (compiled) solver based on "
"SUNDIALS. By exposing the IDAKLU solver to JAX, we provide a fast solver "
"capable of interfacing with third-party JAX-compatible software libraries, "
"such as numpyro."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/idaklu-jax-interface.ipynb:17
msgid ""
"Despite the apparent advantages, there are some limitations to this "
"approach. The most notable is that model derivatives are limited to first-"
"order (i.e. sensitivities), since the IDAKLU solver is not capable of auto-"
"differentiation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/idaklu-jax-interface.ipynb:29
msgid "Setup a basic DFN model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/idaklu-jax-interface.ipynb:31
msgid ""
"To demonstrate use of the IDAKLU-Jax interface, we first set-up a basic "
"model, choosing the DFN model in this case. We will provide two ``inputs`` "
"to the model and will specify a list of variables of interest "
"(``output_variables``). Specifying ``output_variables`` is strongly "
"recommended to reduce computational load, while ``inputs`` are only required "
"when derivatives are to be considered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/idaklu-jax-interface.ipynb:-1
msgid "[1]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/idaklu-jax-interface.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"%pip install \"pybamm[jax]\" -q    # install PyBaMM with JAX support if it "
"is not installed\n"
"import time\n"
"\n"
"import jax\n"
"import jax.numpy as jnp\n"
"import numpy as np\n"
"\n"
"import pybamm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/idaklu-jax-interface.ipynb:59
msgid ""
"<pre>\n"
"Note: you may need to restart the kernel to use updated packages.\n"
"</pre>"
msgstr ""

