#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/idaklu-jax-interface.ipynb:186
msgid ""
"The JAX expression (that we named ``f`` in our example), is a function that "
"can be used and evaluated like any other native JAX expression. This means "
"that it can be included in broader JAX expressions, and can even be JIT "
"compiled. The only limitations are that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/idaklu-jax-interface.ipynb:188
msgid ""
"derivatives cannot be taken beyond first-order, which is the limit of our "
"IDAKLU solver implementation, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/idaklu-jax-interface.ipynb:189
msgid ""
"you are required to specify ``output_variables`` either at the "
"``IDAKLUSolver`` stage, or at the ``jaxify`` stage (you can create many "
"jaxified expressions from a single solver object)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/solvers/idaklu-jax-interface.ipynb:191
msgid "Here is the most basic usage example:"
msgstr ""

